Recommendation
Replace the inverted check:
----new code block----
require(
 !_verify(distroProof, $e.distributionMerkleRoots[epoch], getLeaveUserDistroTree(distro)),
    EpochDistributor_invalidDistroProof()
);
----end of code block ----
with the correct logic:
----new code block----
require(
    _verify(distroProof, $e.distributionMerkleRoots[epoch], getLeaveUserDistroTree(distro)),
    EpochDistributor_invalidDistroProof()
);
----end of code block ----
By removing the negation, valid proofs (
_verify == true
) will pass, and invalid proofs (
_verify == false
) will revert, restoring the intended Merkle proof security.
