dantastisk
@nevillehuang Every epoch
Voter.distribute
(permissionlessly) gets called for every gauge. This calls
Minter.update_period
and the first call to this every epoch will calculate the amount of weekly emissions, mint this amount in flow and transfer it to the Voter contract.
Voter.distribute
then calls
Voter._updateFor
with the gauge address to calculate the share of the weekly emission earned by the gauge. This amount is then transferred to the gauge through a call to
IGauge.notifyRewardAmount
.
ProxyGauge
is used for the weth/flow gauge,
GaugeV4
is used for all other gauges. The weth/flow gauge then
forwards this amount to the flow rewardDistributor
, where it can be claimed.
For all other gauges the reward is claimed directly on the gauge by calling
GaugeV4.getReward
. This function mints oFlow for the liquidity provider by transferring the flow received from the Voter contract.
So, you are correct that oFlow will be minted in the gauge, but the amount minted is equal to the amount of flow received from the Voter contract.
