Vulnerability Report
Context
File:
RecipeOrderbook.sol
Lines:
567, 587
Description
The
forfeit
and
claim
functions in the contract are vulnerable to reentrancy attacks if a reward token has hooks (such as those that implement the ERC777 standard). The reentrancy occurs because the functions perform external calls via
safeTransfer
before clearing the state by deleting the
weirollWalletToLockedRewardParams
mapping. This allows an attacker to reenter the function and drain funds.
