Description
The Node HTTP server, as implemented in the file
http_server.go
, is currently vulnerable to a potential Slowloris attack. This vulnerability stems from the absence of the
ReadHeaderTimeout
setting in the http.Server configuration. The Slowloris attack is a type of Denial of Service (DoS) attack where the attacker sends partial HTTP requests to the server, aiming to open many connections and keep them open as long as possible, thereby exhausting server resources. Without a
ReadHeaderTimeout
, the server lacks a mechanism to time out and close these incomplete request connections, making it susceptible to such attacks.
----new code block----
