The execution does the following:
Calls
depositInitialReserves()
from the malicious hook which essentially deposits and accounts some raw balance into
BunniHub
.
Calls the
hookHandleSwap()
function inside
BunniHub
to withdraw the previously deposited amount.
The
BunniHub
transfers the tokens to the hook.
The
hookHandleSwap()
tries to reach the
targetRawBalance
of token1 and calls the
deposit()
into the malicious vault which forwards the execution back to the malicious hook.
The malicious hook calls the
unlockForRebalance()
function to disable the reentrancy protection.
The malicious hook reenters the
hookHandleSwap()
function the same way as step 2.
Once the function has been re-entered a sufficient number of times to drain all raw balances, the state will be set to 0 instead of decrementing, avoiding an underflow. The end result will be the malicious hook owning all ERC-6909 tokens previously held by the
BunniHub
.
