The value of
interestUsd
parameter is strongly affected by the price returned by
Oracle
. Thus, if the
Oracle
returns a higher value than previously, an integer underflow occurs in
_repay()
function, making debt repayment impossible. To exploit this vulnerability,
_accrueInterest()
must be called prior to
_repay()
to update
interestUsd
parameter.
