Audit Report: StabilityPool Behavior Analysis
Context
(No context files were provided by the reviewer)
Description
The function
StabilityPool.enableCollateral()
will overwrite the old collateral index in case the collateral was sunset. This logic is present in
_overwriteCollateral()
(StabilityPool.sol#L207-L242).
The problem is that it doesn't reset the old value of
lastCollateralError_Offset
in that index. What does this variable mean? It is used to calculate collateral gain per deposit amount, and this specific variable keeps track of the remainder to avoid always rounding down calculations. More details can be found in the comments in StabilityPool.sol#L512-L522.
A similar issue was previously reported, however, the mitigation is insufficient: check 7.3.16 in a Cyfrin report or commit
0915dd49
in Prisma. The problem arises because it uses a non-reset value to round up in the future when recalculating collateral gain during
offset()
. As a result, the total collateral gain distributed will be greater than the actual balance of collateral, meaning that the last user to claim a reward will be unable to do so.
