Impact
When the credit token is ERC20 extensive with hook, such as ERC777 token, the lender can exploit it to draw out extra tokens from borrower's account. And the
count
state variable would also be underflowed, cause the line contract can't be 'REPAID', the borrower will never be able to get back the collateral.
P.S.
Similar attack on imBTC
Proof of Concept
The vulnerable point is in
\_close()
function,
function _close(Credit memory credit, bytes32 id) internal virtual returns (bool) {
    // ...
    if (credit.deposit + credit.interestRepaid > 0) {
        LineLib.sendOutTokenOrETH( // @audit reentrancy attack from here
            credit.token,
            credit.lender,
            credit.deposit + credit.interestRepaid
        );
    }
    // ...
}
The following testcase shows how to exploit it, put it into a new LenderExploit.t.sol file under 'test' directory, it will pass
