The router has been approved as a spender and can therefore transfer
desc.amount
to
desc.srcReceiver
. Subsequently, an external call is made
caller
which is also controlled by the liquidator. Here, they would simply have to perform the swap themselves and transfer the expected amount back to the contract. Keeping any excess. This is an issue for
AggregationRouterV4
and I would expect there are similar types of issues in other DEX aggregator contracts.
AggregationRouterV5
is also vulnerable to the same issue.
