The exposure of an API secret key may lead to significant consequences, as these keys are generally utilized to authenticate and authorize access to an API. Such access may be used to obtain access to sensitive data, conduct actions on behalf of a user, or interact with other systems. For example, in the case of the
qoin_account
, the API secret key is employed to verify the status of an account and generate OTPs.
3. JWT Secrets
