Vulnerability in Aggregator Contract
The
openInterval
function does not update the
aggregator.balance
field. Consequently, subsequent withdrawals may fail due to an inaccurate
aggregator.balance
value, even if there are sufficient funds available within the aggregator.
File Location
contracts/src/Switchboard/aggregator/Aggregator.sol
Solidity Code
----new code block----
function openInterval(address aggregatorId) external payable guarded(4) {
    AggregatorLib.Aggregator storage aggregator = AggregatorLib.aggregators(aggregatorId);
 uint256 reward = OracleQueueLib.oracleQueues(aggregator.queueId).reward;
 if (msg.value < reward * (aggregator.config.minOracleResults + 1)) {
 revert ErrorLib.InsufficientBalance();
    }
    AggregatorLib.refreshInterval(
        aggregatorId,
        reward * (aggregator.config.minOracleResults + 1)
    );
}
----end of code block ----
For instance, this vulnerability may result in an integer overflow during the execution of
withdrawIntervalAndBalance
, potentially resulting in failures of legitimate oracle result post transactions.
