During that transfer, the
distributeAllNFT
function can be called again and again. So multiple transfers will be done for each user.
In addition to that, any receiver of the tokens can revert the transfer. If that happens, nobody will be able to receive their tokens.
Recommendation
Add a reentrancy guard.
Avoid transferring tokens for different receivers in a single transaction.

In the current implementation, after user deposits funds into lending pool and mint lending pool shares, user can call collateralize function to add collateral:
