SuperPositions.onlyMinter() Implementation Issue
Context
SuperPositions.sol#L69-L83
Description
The
SuperPositions.onlyMinter()
function has a faulty implementation, which results in incorrect access control. The issue arises because the current implementation compares the
formImplementationId
instead of the state registry ID for the superform against the state registry ID of
msg.sender
.
Problem
The correct approach should involve retrieving the state registry ID of the superform using the function
getStateRegistryId()
, and then comparing this ID to the ID of
msg.sender
. Due to this incorrect comparison, the implementation fails, leading to any function that utilizes this modifier having improper access control, thereby creating a serious security vulnerability.
A similar issue is present with the modifier
onlyBatchMinter()
.
Recommendation
Make the necessary changes to compare the correct state registry ID as shown below:
----new code block----
modifier onlyMinter(uint256 superformId) {
 address router = superRegistry.getAddress(keccak256("SUPERFORM_ROUTER"));
 // if msg.sender isn't superformRouter then it must be state registry for that superform
 if (msg.sender != router) {
        (, uint32 formBeaconId,) = DataLib.getSuperform(superformId);
        (address superform_, uint32 formImplementationId_, uint64 chainId_) = DataLib.getSuperform(superformId);
 uint8 formRegistryId = ERC4626FormImplementation(superform).getStateRegistryId();
 uint8 registryId = superRegistry.getStateRegistryId(msg.sender);
 if (registryId != formRegistryId) {
 revert Error.NOT_MINTER();
        }
    }
 _;
}
----end of code block ----

