Issue Overview
It was found that it is possible for
multisig.owner_set_seqno
to overflow when updated. This could allow users to propose and execute transactions from an owner set that was previously in use. A sample of the affected code is shown in the snippet below.
Affected Code
----new code block----
pub fn cancel_all_proposals(ctx: Context<Auth>) -> Result<()> {
 let multisig = &mut ctx.accounts.multisig;
 // increment the sequence number
 // so that the pending proposals
 // can no longer be executed
    multisig.owner_set_seqno += 1;
 return Ok(());
}
----end of code block ----
Remediation
Use
checked_add
when updating
multisig.owner_set_seqno
. For more information, refer to the code snippet below.
Remediated Code
----new code block----
pub fn cancel_all_proposals(ctx: Context<Auth>) -> Result<()> {
 let multisig = &mut ctx.accounts.multisig;
 // increment the sequence number
 // so that the pending proposals
 // can no longer be executed
    multisig.owner_set_seqno = multisig.owner_set_seqno.checked_add(1).unwrap();
 return Ok(());
}
----end of code block ----
Patch
Resolved in #278 by using
checked_add
.
